# Chaos Arcade Tower - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
Roguelike + Autobattler + Chess arcade game built with Godot 4.x + C# (.NET).
Source of truth: docs/GDD.docx, docs/TDD.docx, Assets/Game/Data/Configs/Balance/balance_v0_1.yaml

## Architecture
- **Separation**: Domain/Simulation (pure C#, zero Godot deps) vs Presentation (Godot scenes/scripts)
- **Data-driven**: Pieces, perks, rarities, drop tables live in JSON configs under Assets/Game/Data/
- **Determinism**: ALL randomness through SeededRandomService. Same seed => same result. No System.Random direct usage.
- **Composition over inheritance**: Perks/effects as composable components, not deep class hierarchies.
- **State machines**: Explicit FSMs for game flow and combat phases.

## Coding Standards (C#)
- **Naming**: PascalCase for types/methods/properties, camelCase for locals/params, _camelCase for private fields, UPPER_SNAKE for constants
- **Namespaces**: Match folder structure (ChaosArcadeTower.Domain.Pieces, etc.)
- **No God classes**: Max ~200 lines per class. Split by system/responsibility.
- **SOLID-ish**: Interfaces for services (ICombatResolver, ISaveService, etc.), single responsibility per class.
- **Immutable where possible**: PieceDefinition, PerkDefinition are read-only data. Runtime state is PieceInstance, PerkInstance.
- **No public fields**: Use properties. Exception: simple data structs for serialization.

## Determinism Requirements
- All combat logic uses IRandomService (seeded).
- Piece action order: deterministic by (slotIndex, side). Process: collect ready pieces, sort, resolve in order.
- Status effects, perk hooks, and timed events processed in fixed order.
- Never use DateTime.Now or Environment.TickCount in simulation.

## MVP Constraints
- NO online multiplayer.
- NO complex economy (gold/shop/leveling) beyond perks + bot generation.
- NO scope creep: if a feature isn't in TDD milestones, it doesn't get built.
- Prefer data-driven content. Tuning lives in JSON/YAML configs, not hardcoded.
- TODO markers allowed ONLY if they don't block MVP completion.

## File Organization
```
src/Core/         - Interfaces, utilities, RNG, event bus
src/Domain/       - Pure models: Piece, Perk, Board, Run, Combat
src/Simulation/   - Combat engine, effects, scoring, target selection
src/AI/           - Bot run simulator, positioning heuristics
src/Presentation/ - Godot scenes, UI controllers, game flow
src/Infrastructure/ - Save/load, config loading, balance services
Assets/Game/Data/ - JSON/YAML configs (balance, perks, pieces)
```

## Definition of Done (per milestone)
- [ ] Game launches and runs without errors
- [ ] All buttons/navigation work (no dead ends)
- [ ] New features are testable in-game
- [ ] Determinism: same seed produces same combat result
- [ ] No monolithic classes (>200 lines = split)
- [ ] Code compiles with zero warnings

## Godot Conventions
- Scene names: PascalCase.tscn
- One controller script per scene (attached to root node)
- Use signals for UI events, EventBus for cross-system communication
- GetNode<T> for child references with [Export] or explicit paths
